<title>MONACO: TENNIS-MONTE CARLO OPEN RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-MONTE CARLO OPEN RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>MONTE CARLO 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second round results in the</p>
<p>$2.3 million Monte Carlo men's tennis Open on Wednesday (prefix</p>
<p>number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>4-Richard Krajicek (Netherlands) beat Michael Stich (Germany)</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>6-0</p>
<p>Carlos Costa (Spain) beat 8-Wayne Ferreira (South Africa) 6-4</p>
<p>7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>Emilio Alvarez (Spain) beat 14-Alberto Berasategui (Spain) 6-3</p>
<p>3-6 6-4</p>
<p>Mark Philippoussis (Australia) beat 13-Jim Courier (U.S.) 7-5</p>
<p>7-5</p>
<p>10-Albert Costa (Spain) beat Slava Dosedel (Czech Republic) 6-3</p>
<p>6-3</p>
<p>Bohdan Ulihrach (Czech Republic) beat 5-Thomas Enqvist (Sweden)</p>
<p>7-5 4-6 6-3</p>
<p>Christian Ruud (Norway) beat 3-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia) 6-4</p>
<p>2-6</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>12-Alex Corretja (Spain) beat Cedric Pioline (France) 6-4 6-3</p>
<p>Andrei Medvedev (Ukraine) beat 11-Felix Mantilla (Spain) 6-2</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic) beat 15-Marc Rosset (Switzerland)</p>
<p>7-6 (7-5) 6-1</p>
<p>7-Marcelo Rios (Chile) beat Andrea Gaudenzi (Italy) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>16-Sergi Bruguera (Spain) beat Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) 6-4</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>Arnaud Boestch (France) beat Renzo Furlan (Italy) 3-6 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>6-Carlos Moya (Spain) beat Francisco Clavet (Spain) 6-1 4-6 6-1</p>
</text>
